{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Final rebar-debug repair evidence (pre-Gerrit). Problem: two individual tests used production-scale real-time values and contributed 15–25s long poles despite parallel execution. Proven mechanisms were already recorded in Phase 1: the progressing snapshot test used a 10s low-speed window with a 15s real server; the ACLI terminal-read test used a 1s per-attempt deadline plus real 2s/4s logical backoffs.\n\nHeld-out proof: /tmp/rebar_short_window_oracle.py was RED on current main for both exact nodes. The fixer was isolated from that oracle. After repair, both nodes were GREEN in 3.88s. Defect-seeded mutations independently restored the socket values to window=10/server=15 and the ACLI deadline to 1s; each returned the held-out oracle to RED for the exact expected assertion, then restoration returned GREEN.\n\nFix: the snapshot test injects a 1s window and serves above the floor for 2s through the same real loopback socket. The ACLI test installs 0.1s call/grace/drain values during fixture setup, records logical backoff [2,4] without sleeping, wraps the real parent-side Popen only to record every returned PID, retains exactly _MAX_ATTEMPTS real child sessions, and polls until all are absent. Production defaults, attempts, process-group cleanup, socket semantics, coverage, and assertions remain intact; there is no wall-clock pass threshold, skip, xfail, dependency, or runner change.\n\nReplication: the snapshot node is about 2.10s and ACLI call phase about 0.31s; both complete files pass 20 tests in 11.66s. Ruff check/format and diff-check pass. Caller/sibling scope is test-only; the production timing/config surfaces are untouched and no parity gap applies. OSS consensus references and tracker rejection cross-check remain in the ticket description/comments."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786649939036489001,"uuid":"18f58f67-305b-43c2-903e-05367913da49"}